cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the paper and the software."
title: "Reflexivity in Options Markets"
abstract: >-
  A continuous-time Heston-like stochastic-volatility model in which the
  underlying spot price is coupled to its own option market through a
  dealer-gamma feedback channel. Includes a 3D reflexive SDE simulator,
  four non-reflexive baselines, an arbitrage-free surface filter, an RL
  training infrastructure (ATLAS / Mamba + PPO + BC + EWC), a Hopf
  bifurcation theorem with closed-form first Lyapunov coefficient for
  log-normal open-interest in moneyness, and a pre-registered evaluation
  framework (sliced Wasserstein-2 on IV surfaces, kappa-sensitivity slope,
  Hopf-frequency spectral test).
